<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch-number-theory" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Number Theory</title>

  <introduction>
     <p>
    The study of the integers and their properties forms part of the area of
    mathematics called Number Theory. The topic forms the basis for almost all
    modern day computing. It is used in ATMs, mobile phones, WIFI, televisions,
    radio broadcasting, all of the music mediums (such as CDs, and all the file
    formats such as MP3, OGG, WAV, AIFF etc), dvds, space transmissions, and
    secure electronic data storage and compression.
  </p>

  <p>
    In this chapter we shall concentrate on the properties of integers in
    relation to division and multiplication, but it is worth remembering that
    even the basic ideas developed here are fundamental to all of the
    applications just mentioned. Indeed, the concept of modular arithmetic alone
    touches on practically all of the applications just mentioned.
  </p>
  </introduction>

